        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0fdfa281-b870-51b6-ac32-4dde71b0657a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Piet Norval, Wayne Ferreira, Emilio Sánchez, Kevin Ullyett\n- Events: 1988 Olympic Games, 1992 Summer Olympics, 2000 Stockholm Open\n- Competitions: men's doubles, doubles competition, wheelchair tennis events, Davis Cup\n\nFacts:\n- Emilio Sánchez won three Grand Slam doubles titles and the men's doubles silver medal at the 1988 Olympic Games.\n- Piet Norval represented his native country in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona, where he partnered Wayne Ferreira.\n- Piet Norval and Kevin Ullyett were the defending champions at the 2000 Stockholm Open doubles event, but they lost in the semifinals.\n- Emilio Sánchez captained his nation to Davis Cup success in 2008 after retiring.\n- In 2012, Emilio Sánchez was a tournament director for two wheelchair tennis events.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bc46caf2-8170-5ee0-a44e-ee2d51aef2a9",
        "text": "Page: Piet Norval. Sentence: The right-hander represented his native country in the doubles competition at the 1992 Summer Olympics in Barcelona, where he partnered Wayne Ferreira.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: He won three Grand Slam doubles titles and the men's doubles silver medal at the 1988 Olympic Games.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: Sanchez since retiring captained his nation to Davis Cup success in 2008.\nPage: Emilio Sánchez. Sentence: In 2012 Sanchez was a tournament director for two wheelchair tennis events.\nPage: 2000 Stockholm Open – Doubles. Sentence: Piet Norval and Kevin Ullyett were the defending champions, but lost in the semifinals this year.",
